+def _tag_failed_api_key(exc: BaseException, client: Any) -> None:
+    """Record on ``exc`` the API key of the client whose request raised it.
+
+    The post-rotation retry builds its own client from the (rotated) pool, so
+    the caller cannot know which key it sent. Without the tag, recovery of a
+    retry failure has no key identity and the pool marks whatever its cursor
+    happens to point at — potentially a healthy key.
